WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.167
The FDA says a

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.302
popular ingredient

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.603
in many over-the-counter

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.805
medicines for colds and allergies

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.207
doesn't work.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.142
Concluding in a panel this week

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.611
that the main ingredient in those drugs

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.813
is ineffective in tablet form.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:14.481
Phenol.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:16.082
Ephron is used in products

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.085
like Benadryl, allergy plus congestion,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.721
Sudafed PE and Vicks snacks,

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.089
according to the FDA.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:23.656
These products

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:27.160
generally nearly generated rather nearly

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.064
$1.8 billion in sales last year alone.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:31.598
Dr.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.233
Jane Morgan, a cardiologist,

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.267
joining me right now.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.301
Dr. Morgan, good to see you.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.871
So a lot of doctors have questioned

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.740
the effectiveness of

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.910
Ephron final Ephron for a very long time.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.512
So how did it find its way

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.379
in these products?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.647
And so, you know,

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.548
that was approved

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.983
back in 1972,

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.584
where the criteria was

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.053
a little less stringent.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:53.820
But we started to

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.188
have some pushback against it

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.357
around 2006, 2007

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.892
and then 2016

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.895
really started generating data to refute

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:05.065
the original claims in 1972.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:05.865
And so it's really

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.301
come to this point here in 2023

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.170
with finally looking at that data

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.671
and saying, you know what?

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.073
It really doesn't work.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.774
It's not any better than placebo

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.177
in the oral formulation.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.179
The reason for that is

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.548
if you take it by mouth in any form

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:22.615
your liver

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.818
and gut metabolize, in other words

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.853
degrade it to such a degree

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.720
until there's

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.190
not much active compound left.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.025
So it still takes way.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.625
That's right.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.694
You can still take the nasal spray

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.196
but you cannot take anything orally.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:36.763
Okay.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.766
So do you see that drug even

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.601
being reclassified

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.403
as a result of this discovery

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.004
or acknowledgment?

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.106
And so we will wait

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.308
for the comment portion of the FDA

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.176
and then their final ruling on

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.177
whether or not

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.980
they will actually ask companies

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.316
to reformulate their products

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.051
or whether it will be a total recall

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:58.952
and say all of these

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.054
have to be removed from the shelves.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:01.688
Remember,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.189
this is an entire industry there.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.291
Over 250 products

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.560
over the counter that contain phenol.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.029
And so it's going to be very impactful.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.131
But we also have to have

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.365
products available

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.433
that are effective

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.602
and actually do what we say

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.236
they're going to do.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:16.302
Well,

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.270
I wonder what that's going to

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.305
how that will impact consumers.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.874
I mean, when you have a cold,

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.142
you have symptoms

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.477
related to a cold or flu or something

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.879
to those degrees,

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.247
you generally

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.381
going to reach

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.116
for some of these products.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.318
But now there may be some reticence

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.587
about trusting any of them,

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.755
even if they don't have

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.056
this ingredient in them.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.092
You know, I have an opposing view.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.493
We should actually have

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.795
more confidence in our system now

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.197
because we have the ability

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:44.964
to go back and say,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.599
you know what, we made a mistake

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.367
and you know what?

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.435
Things have changed in 50 years,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.104
and we're going to acknowledge

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.672
that science has advanced

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.541
and that we have new information

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.441
and we're going to act

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.809
on that information.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.611
If, in fact, you have a cold,

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.913
you can ask for products

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.081
that have pseudoephedrine in them.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.483
Those are over the counter.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.951
But behind the counter,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.986
you have to ask the pharmacist for them.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.321
You don't need a prescription

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.722
because they do have value

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.591
in making street meth,

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.425
also products

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.194
with glass, venison in them.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:16.262
And so those are still ingredients

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.498
that are very effective

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.333
for people who have nasal congestion.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.201
So there is still

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.203
some good stuff out there, you say.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.037
Okay, now

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:26.606
a big concern, of course, this fall

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.840
and of course, this winter

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.276
as we're spending more time inside

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.178
COVID and the latest strain

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.479
there is a new COVID

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.748
vaccine already on the market. Right.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.183
When do we start getting that?

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.152
So that vaccine is available now.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.286
And in fact, we saw

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.087
the FDA

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:41.588
say that

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.756
this really should be broadly available

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.457
to everybody.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.125
Six months of age and older.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.027
And then the CDC came behind them

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.062
and supported it

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.230
and said universally

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.397
this should be available.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.131
We thought that

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.499
originally it was only going

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.668
to be targeted to immunocompromised

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.836
and specialized groups.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:57.904
That was an option.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.539
But it'll be universally available

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.841
and is available right now.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.643
As of yesterday to everyone

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.711
age, months and older,

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.079
six months and older.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:08.014
And we'll see it be broadly available

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.148
now that manufacturing

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.316
will really ramp up

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.318
in the next week or two. All right.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.153
Get those shots.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.955
Once again here we go.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:16.256
All right.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.790
Dr. Jane Morgan, great to see you.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.825
Nice to see you. Thanks for.

